// Title: Renamed FTP.EXE Execution
// Sigma ID: 277a4393-446c-449a-b0ed-7fdc7795244c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Victor Sergeev, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-09 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059, T1202
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed "ftp.exe" binary based on the PE metadata fields
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Ftp/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_ftp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ftp.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\ftp.exe"))
